// The first wake, 2039: the night in her house, room by room, until the eulogy at dawn.
//
// The rooms mechanic moves her two hours at a time and sets `room` and `hour`; at each
// move it asks the pool for what happens there and then. The most specific candidate
// that holds wins, so a line that also needs what the day kept beats a plain one.

== wake                                          # rooms · rooms front, kitchen, stairs · hours 20, 22, 0, 2, 4, 6 · pool wake_night · then dawn
{ life = stay: The front room. Everyone she ever kept is here. | The front room of the flat by the river. Everyone she ever met on purpose is here. }
{ life = stay: A man | A woman } nobody knows stands at the foot of the coffin. { life = stay: He | She } has been there since eight.
{ life = stay }
  MARGARET: Who is he?                            # who her sister
  TOM: Mum never said anything about a cousin.    # who her eldest
  GOT_ON: you know exactly who he is.
{ life = go }
  MARTIN: Who is she? One of your mother's students?
  LEO: Mum never mentioned a —                    # who her son
  STAYED: you know exactly who she is.

== wake_night (pool)
// the front room
= reading_glasses   when { room = front and hour = 22 and life = stay }
  DANNY: Forty-one years. She'd say forty-three. She counted the courting.   # who her husband
  Someone has put her reading glasses on the coffin, folded, as if she might want them.
= rain              when { room = front and hour = 22 and life = go }
  MARTIN: We parted kindly. She sent me recordings of rain. I have two hundred and six.
= same_hands        when { room = front and hour = 0 }
  The stranger is back at the coffin, looking at the photograph on the easel.
  STRANGER: Same hands.                           # known hands
  { life = stay } GOT_ON: he means yours. your father's.
  { life = go }   STAYED: she means yours. your father's.
= cake              when { room = front and hour = 2 and life = stay and kept has danny }
  The front room is asleep in its chairs. Danny isn't.
  DANNY: She made me a cake every year. Every year it sank. There's one in the freezer. I can't.
= birthday          when { room = front and hour = 2 and life = stay }
  The front room is asleep in its chairs. Danny isn't.
  DANNY: She missed my birthday in '98. Her dad was dying. I've never once held it against her. I've thought about it every year.
= the_river         when { room = front and hour = 2 and life = go and kept has walk }
  The front room is asleep in its chairs. Martin isn't.
  MARTIN: She walked by the river every morning. If you came with her, you weren't allowed to talk. I came for nine years.
= no_hour           when { room = front and hour = 2 and life = go }
  The front room is asleep in its chairs. Martin isn't.
  MARTIN: She never had an hour to herself. She said so at Leo's wedding, into the microphone. Everyone laughed. She didn't.
= empty_room        when { room = front and hour = 4 }
  The front room is empty except for her. The candles have burned down to the brass.
  The front door is open a hand's width. The stranger has gone.

// the kitchen
= where_she_hid     when { room = kitchen and hour = 20 }
  { spot = stairs }  MARGARET: She hid under our stairs every single time. I always found her first. I let her think it was luck.
  { spot = piano }   MARGARET: She hid behind Dad's piano once. I walked past three times. I could hear her breathing. I let her stay.
  { spot = door }    MARGARET: She hid at the kitchen door once and heard something about Dad. She was gentler with him after.
  { spot = landing } MARGARET: She hid on the landing once and fell asleep there. I stopped looking. I've never told anyone that.
  { life = go } Margaret came down on the train. She looks at the flat as if it might be a trick.
= sandwiches        when { room = kitchen and hour = 22 and life = stay }
  The stranger is by the kettle with a cup he hasn't drunk.
  JOAN: Are you family, love?
  STRANGER: Yes. — No. Not here.
  JOAN: Well. There's sandwiches.
= never_learned     when { room = kitchen and hour = 22 and life = go }
  The stranger is by the kettle with a cup she hasn't drunk.
  A STUDENT: Did she teach you too?
  STRANGER: No. I never learned. There was a piano, but it was shut.
= with_dad          when { room = kitchen and hour = 0 and kept has dad }
  MARGARET: She was with Dad at the end. He told her something. She never said what.
= without_dad       when { room = kitchen and hour = 0 }
  MARGARET: She didn't make it to Dad. He asked for her twice. I never told her that. Well. I can't now.
= two_of_you        when { room = kitchen and hour = 2 }
  ->> stranger_talk
= washed_cup        when { room = kitchen and hour = 4 }
  The cup is washed and upside down on the rack. The back door is on the latch.

// the stairs
= in_the_box        when { room = stairs and hour = 20 and life = stay }
  Three grandchildren on the stairs, in the order they sat down.
  THE YOUNGEST: Is Gran in the box?
  THE ELDEST: Gran's in the box.
= one_hand          when { room = stairs and hour = 20 and life = go and kept has rehearsal }
  Musicians on the stairs, cases between their knees.
  A CELLIST: She stopped us once with one hand. I've never been so frightened or so happy.
= too_fast          when { room = stairs and hour = 20 and life = go }
  Musicians on the stairs, cases between their knees.
  A CELLIST: We play her second movement too fast. Everyone does now. She wasn't there to stop us, that once, and it stuck.
= the_final         when { room = stairs and hour = 22 and life = stay and kept has tom }
  TOM: She came to the final in '98. Stood up the whole second half. I've never been so ashamed. Best day of my life.
= the_gap           when { room = stairs and hour = 22 and life = stay }
  TOM: She missed the final in '98. I scored. I looked up and there was a gap where she should've been. I still look up.
= the_tree          when { room = stairs and hour = 22 and life = go and kept has leo }
  LEO: She came to see me be a tree. She said I was the best tree. I was the only tree.
= very_still        when { room = stairs and hour = 22 and life = go }
  LEO: I was a tree in the school play in '98. She was at a rehearsal. I stayed very still so she'd be proud anyway.
= the_fever         when { room = stairs and hour = 0 and life = stay and kept has ruth }
  RUTH: I had a fever the day of Tom's final. She stayed with me. I've never told him I was glad.
= the_door          when { room = stairs and hour = 0 and life = stay }
  RUTH: I had a fever the day of Tom's final. I watched the door all morning. I still watch doors.
= the_bow           when { room = stairs and hour = 0 and life = go and kept has premiere }
  A VIOLINIST: She took the bow at her own premiere and walked straight out of the building. Nobody knows where she went.
= on_a_train        when { room = stairs and hour = 0 and life = go }
  A VIOLINIST: She missed her own premiere. She was on a train. The conductor took her bow and has been insufferable ever since.
= eight_bars        when { room = stairs and hour = 2 and life = stay and kept has piano }
  ELLIE: She played at my wedding. Eight bars, over and over. Nobody minded.   # who her youngest
= never_heard       when { room = stairs and hour = 2 and life = stay }
  ELLIE: There was a piano in this house my whole life, and I never once heard it.
= a_kitchen         when { room = stairs and hour = 2 and life = go and kept has radio }
  LEO: She always told the radio her music came from a kitchen. I never knew which kitchen.
= to_the_room       when { room = stairs and hour = 2 and life = go }
  LEO: Nobody rang her for years, at the end. She played anyway. To the room.
= asleep            when { room = stairs and hour = 4 }
  The children have fallen asleep on the stairs, in the order they sat down.
// nothing for this room at this hour
= nothing           when { true }
  Nothing happens here for two hours. Somebody laughs in another room and stops.

// Two in the morning, in the kitchen: the only one who looks at where you are.
== stranger_talk                                 # talk
Just the two of you: the stranger, and you, in a way.
{ life = stay: He | She } looks straight at where you are.
- (ask)
* Who are you?
  ~ met = true
  STRANGER: Someone she never met.
  -> ask
* How did you know her?
  ~ met = true
  STRANGER: She wouldn't know me. I knew her once. In a way.
  -> ask
* You're { life = stay: her son | her daughter }.    # voice · told "by your other self"
  ~ met = true
  A long time.
  STRANGER: Not in this one.
  -> ask
* Let { life = stay: him | her } be.
  { life = stay: He | She } goes back to the window. Neither of you says anything else.
  <-

== dawn                                          # card
Dawn. They carry the chairs back to the kitchen. { life = stay: Tom | Leo } stands by the coffin with a folded page.
->> eulogy
* Go back                                        # choose · picture title
  -> her_life
* Let her rest here
  -> rest
